<title>USA: Dotronix to buy back 250,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Dotronix to buy back 250,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRIGHTON, Minn. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dotronix Inc said Monday it plans to buy back as many as 250,000 of its shares from time to time on the open market.</p>
<p>The company, which designs and manufactures high resolution video displays, has about 4.3 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
